<title>HONG KONG: HK&amp;Shanghai Hotels up after rights issue.</title>
<headline>HK&amp;Shanghai Hotels up after rights issue.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hong Kong and Shanghai Hotels Ltd shrugged off news that the company planned a rights issue, rising HK$0.20 to HK$14.05 in Friday morning trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The rights issue news seems neutral since the (rights issue) proportion of one-for-12 is relatively small and the free warrant attached makes the issue more attractive,&quot; said Michael Ng, dealing manager at Sassoon Securities.</p>
<p>Investors were covering positions after the shares fell to a low of HK$13.60 in early trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>-- HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 2843 6369</p>
